WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.067
Feature engineering.

2
00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.993
Models only see numbers.

3
00:00:03.993 --> 00:00:08.533
Your job is to turn raw columns into signals they can actually use.

4
00:00:09.733 --> 00:00:12.700
A model has no idea what a planet or a star is.

5
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.167
It cannot invent domain knowledge from raw columns alone.

6
00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:20.833
So you add that knowledge yourself, as new derived columns called features.

7
00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:24.433
Here is the same data, before and after.

8
00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:29.967
A raw timestamp is nearly useless, but hour, weekday and weekend flag can be gold.

9
00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:36.267
Mass and radius alone say little, yet their ratio is density, which has real physical meaning.

10
00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:39.733
A log of the orbital period tames huge ranges.

11
00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:41.800
Same information, new shape.

12
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.033
There are four recipes you will use again and again.

13
00:00:46.333 --> 00:00:49.000
Ratios and interactions between columns.

14
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.900
Time components pulled from a single timestamp.

15
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.567
Aggregations, like a star's average planet radius.

16
00:00:55.867 --> 00:00:59.200
And domain flags, booleans that encode an expert's rule.

17
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:01.733
Here it is in pandas.

18
00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:04.127
Each line creates one new column.

19
00:01:04.127 --> 00:01:11.233
Density is mass divided by radius cubed, and temperature is compared to Earth's two hundred eighty eight kelvin.

20
00:01:11.533 --> 00:01:14.533
Then a flag marks planets that are roughly Earth sized.

21
00:01:15.733 --> 00:01:17.833
Now the payoff on a real project.

22
00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:23.267
A first classifier on raw columns plateaus at zero point eight one AUC.

23
00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:28.100
The gradient boosted upgrade you planned would buy about zero point zero two.

24
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:34.900
Adding density, log period and temperature ratio jumps it to zero point eight eight, in an afternoon.

25
00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:36.906
Let's recap.

26
00:01:36.906 --> 00:01:40.800
Feature engineering turns raw columns into usable signals.

27
00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:44.167
It injects domain knowledge the model cannot invent.

28
00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:47.800
Think ratios, time parts, aggregations and flags.

29
00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.358
And it often beats a fancier model.

30
00:01:50.358 --> 00:01:52.100
Next up: feature selection.
